+/// A marker never reaches a collector: the daemon writes it before the
+/// corresponding `spool_gap` is durable and unlinks it afterwards.  Its schema
+/// still lives beside the wire records so that every stack reads the same
+/// field names, order and encoding, and so the shared golden vectors can pin
+/// the exact bytes.  Numbers are plain JSON integers here, unlike the decimal
+/// strings of the exported `spool_gap`.
